<interrogationes unitas="widget">

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I put several widgets in one window and route keys and clicks to them?
    <responsum symbolum="manager_widget_creare manager_widget_registrare manager_widget_tractare_eventum manager_widget_reddere">Create
      a ManagerWidget with manager_widget_creare(piscina), register
      each widget with its datum, a FunctioReddere, a
      FunctioTractareEventum and a rectangle in CHARACTER cells
      (manager_widget_registrare), then call
      manager_widget_tractare_eventum for every event and
      manager_widget_reddere every frame. Widgets are painted in
      registration order, each told whether it has focus. schirmata.c
      and layout.c are the in-tree users. The header's EXEMPLUM shows
      an older registrare call with no reddere or tractare_eventum
      arguments; follow the prototype instead.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can I register more than sixteen widgets with one manager?
    <responsum symbolum="manager_widget_registrare ManagerWidget">No.
      The manager holds a fixed array of XVI Widget slots and
      manager_widget_registrare returns -1 when it is full (or the
      manager is NIHIL). Check that return value: layout.c ignores it,
      so a seventeenth widget would silently never draw or receive
      events. There is no call to unregister or replace a widget:
      schirmata.c swaps one by writing the datum, reddere and
      tractare_eventum fields of manager-&gt;widgets[i]
      directly.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how does focus move between widgets?
    <responsum symbolum="manager_widget_ponere_focus manager_widget_focus_proximum manager_widget_focus_praecedens manager_widget_focus_ad_punctum manager_widget_tractare_eventum" via="lib/fenestra_macos.m">The
      first widget registered gets focus. A mouse-down focuses the
      first widget whose cell rectangle contains the click
      (manager_widget_focus_ad_punctum), and a Tab key the focused
      widget did not consume moves focus to the next widget, wrapping
      (manager_widget_focus_proximum). The manager checks only that the
      key is CLAVIS_TABULA, never the modifiers, and the macOS
      fenestra maps the Tab key to CLAVIS_TABULA with or without
      Shift, so an unconsumed Shift-Tab also moves focus FORWARD: to go
      back, consume Shift-Tab in your widget and call
      manager_widget_focus_praecedens. A click outside every widget
      leaves focus where it was, and the event still goes to the
      focused widget. Out-of-range indices to ponere_focus are
      ignored.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can I rely on click-to-focus when the font is drawn at scale 2 or more?
    <responsum symbolum="manager_widget_tractare_eventum manager_widget_reddere">No.
      manager_widget_reddere passes your scala to the widgets, but
      manager_widget_tractare_eventum converts the mouse position to
      cells with a fixed six by eight pixels (scale I), so at any
      other scale clicks focus the wrong widget. The only in-tree
      renderer (concha via schirmata_reddere) draws at scale
      I.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I detect a double click in a widget?
    <responsum symbolum="manager_widget_tractare_eventum">The
      manager does it: a mouse-down within DUPLEX_CLICK_TEMPUS (0.3 s)
      and DUPLEX_CLICK_DISTANTIA (XII pixels) of the previous one is
      delivered to the focused widget as EVENTUS_MUS_DUPLEX INSTEAD of
      EVENTUS_MUS_DEPRESSUS, so the widget does not see a second
      press. The timer then resets, so a third click starts a new
      pair. Mouse coordinates reach the widget in window pixels, not
      relative to the widget.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quid">
    <quaestio! (>what is a ContextusWidget and does the manager use it?
    <responsum symbolum="contextus_widget_creare ContextusWidget">A
      bundle of shared services handed to widget constructors and
      factories: piscina, intern, and optionally the entity
      repository, command registry, widget registry and a mode-switch
      callback. contextus_widget_creare returns NIHIL only when
      piscina or intern is NIHIL. The ManagerWidget never reads it; it
      only needs a piscina.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

</interrogationes>
